The chart uses the framework's `Concept` type in six modules, all as type-only imports from `@openmrs/esm-framework`. The only runtime code that reads its shape is `mapConcept` and `getConceptCode` in the form-entry app. A behaviour change in the framework could therefore affect those modules' data handling, and it could also affect the chart's `NumericObservation` consumers, which depend on the framework's concept reference-range behaviour.

**Framework definition**
- The `Concept` interface is defined at openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-api/src/types/concept-resource.ts:4-18. It has `name`, `datatype`, `conceptClass`, `set`, `names`, `mappings`, `answers`, `setMembers` and related fields.

**Chart code that uses `Concept`, most likely affected first**
1. `mapConcept` and `getConceptCode` in the form-entry data source. `getConceptCode` reads `concept.mappings` and the `conceptReferenceTerm` shape, and `mapConcept` reads `concept.name.display` and `concept.uuid`. Any change to the mappings or name shape would break these directly. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-data-source/form-data-source.service.ts:28-38} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-data-source/form-data-source.service.ts:347-363}
2. The `Concept` import in the same file. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-form-entry-app/src/app/form-data-source/form-data-source.service.ts:13}
3. Order posting, where `Concept` types the order's `concept` field. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/orders/postOrders.ts:1-10} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-common-lib/src/orders/postOrders.ts:132}
4. The horizontal obs table, which types its `concepts` props with `Concept`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-generic-patient-widgets-app/src/obs-table-horizontal/obs-table-horizontal.component.tsx:13} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-generic-patient-widgets-app/src/obs-table-horizontal/obs-table-horizontal.component.tsx:274}
5. The tablet lab-results helper, which reads `Concept` metadata. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/individual-results-table-tablet/helper.tsx:3} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/individual-results-table-tablet/helper.tsx:83-90}
6. The lab panel data hook, which types the SWR response as `Concept`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/individual-results-table-tablet/usePanelData.tsx:6} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/individual-results-table-tablet/usePanelData.tsx:74-82}
7. The visit-notes resource, which fetches concepts as `Concept`. @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes.resource.ts:9} and @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/notes/visit-notes.resource.ts:105}

**Chart code affected through `NumericObservation`**
The framework's `NumericObservation` component (esm-styleguide) resolves concept reference ranges from a `conceptUuid`, so it is affected if the framework's concept behaviour changes. The chart passes `conceptUuid` in these places:
- @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/vitals/paginated-vitals.component.tsx:99-130}
- @file:{github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart::packages/esm-patient-vitals-app/src/biometrics/paginated-biometrics.component.tsx:94}
